      },
      "author": [
        "ACME"
      ],
      "description": "Detects a successful (200/206) GET over unencrypted HTTP where the URL ends in an executable or script extension (exe, dll, ps1, bat, cmd, vbs, hta, scr, msi, jar). Windows Update / Delivery Optimization traffic, which produces most such downloads (via msdownload / filestreamingservice paths and Microsoft ASNs), is excluded. Plain-HTTP binaries are a common malware delivery and tool-transfer channel and can be tampered with in transit. Baseline on 2026-10-05: ~3 matching events per 10 minutes after exclusions.",
