        ]
      },
      "language": "lucene",
      "license": "",
      "max_signals": 100,
      "meta": {
        "created_from": "CC_Report_Writer proxy baseline 2026-10-05"
      },
      "note": "### Investigation Steps\n1. Review `url.original` and `destination.domain` / `destination.ip`. Is it a known vendor download site (e.g. software-dl.ti.com, dl.google.com) or an unknown IP/host?\n2. Check `destination.as.organization.name`, `destination.geo.country_name`, and whether the same URL was fetched by many hosts (patching) or one host (targeted).\n3. If the file came from a raw IP or a recently registered domain, obtain the file hash from the endpoint and check VirusTotal.\n4. `http.response.status_code: 206` with many requests = resumable download, normal for updaters.\n\n### False positives\nSoftware updaters that still use HTTP (TI Code Composer, some Linux repos, Java tooling). Add trusted domains to the exception list.",
      "query": "network.protocol:http AND http.request.method:GET AND http.response.status_code:(200 OR 206) AND url.original.keyword:/.*\\.([Ee][Xx][Ee]|[Dd][Ll][Ll]|[Pp][Ss]1|[Bb][Aa][Tt]|[Cc][Mm][Dd]|[Vv][Bb][Ss]|[Hh][Tt][Aa]|[Ss][Cc][Rr]|[Mm][Ss][Ii]|[Jj][Aa][Rr])(\\?.*)?/ AND NOT url.original.keyword:*msdownload* AND NOT url.original.keyword:*windowsupdate* AND NOT url.original.keyword:*filestreamingservice* AND NOT destination.as.organization.name.keyword:\"Microsoft Corporation\"",
